//! The TCPP02-M18 USB Type-C protection IC for source applications, STMicroelectronics, in the
//! 18-pin QFN package (3.5 x 3.5 x 0.55 mm, 0.5 mm pitch, exposed pad), order code TCPP02-M18:
//! the U5 of the Power Manifold charger module (the board's footprint is `Local Library:
//! QFN-18_L3.5-W3.5-P0.50-TL-EP2.2` and the LCSC number it carries, C3662929, is the
//! TCPP02-M18).
//!
//! The pin table was WRITTEN BY HAND from ST's datasheet "TCPP02-M18: USB Type-C protection for
//! source application" (DS13787 Rev 4, May 2022, 27 pages, the copy that LCSC links for C3662929,
//! fetched on 2026-11-11 from
//! <https://datasheet.lcsc.com/datasheet/pdf/3ad4428212a3b17bacf09a5a8bdbe7b1.pdf>, SHA-256
//! `291a75882c46`): Figure 1 "QFN-18L 3.5 x 3.5 x 0.55 mm (top view)" and Table 1 "Pinout and
//! functions" (printed page 2) for the pad numbers, names, types and descriptions. The datasheet
//! is copyrighted (STMicroelectronics): only facts are taken here (numbers, names, kinds).
//!
//! The exposed pad is `GND`, which the table numbers `EP` and Figure 1 prints as pin 19: pad 19
//! here (it is the number of the reference board's footprint too), one pin with the pads 10 and
//! 14. The kinds follow Table 1's type column: `Input` (`EN`, `SRC`, `VBUSc`, `Isense`,
//! `I2C_ADD`) is `input`, `Output` (`IANA`, `GATE`, `CBIAS`, `FLGn`) is `output`, `Input /
//! Output` (`CC1`, `CC2`, `CC1c`, `CC2c`, `SDA`, `SCL`) is `bidirectional`, `Power`
//! (`VCC_VCONN`) and `GND` are `power`. `FLGn` is "open-drain output flag (active low), floating
//! when not connected": an `output`, and a board may leave it open. `CBIAS` is "ESD capacitor":
//! the capacitor's pin, an `output` as the table says.
//!
//! The supply is a rail, `.vcc`: `.vcc.pos` is `VCC_VCONN` (pad 3) and `.vcc.neg` the `GND` pads
//! (10, 14 and 19), with the datasheet's recommended window: Table 4 "Recommended operating
//! condition" (printed page 5) 2.7 V minimum and 5.5 V maximum for `VCC_VCONN` (the pin
//! description says "connect to 3.3 V or 5.5 V"). The other rows of Table 4 are not stated
//! (`EN`, `IANA`, `I2C_ADD`, `SDA`, `SCL` and `FLGn` 1.7 V to 3.6 V; `CC1c`, `CC2c`, `VBUSc`,
//! `Isense` and `SRC` 0 V to 22 V).
//!
//! Three numbers of the datasheet are stated, for the board to relate to its own parts (the
//! part has no model of its function and no `dc` statement):
//!
//! - the supply current, Table 5 "Electrical characteristics - Power supply" (printed page 6):
//!   `ICC_VCONN` 2.7 mA at most in normal mode and 1 uA at most in low power mode, so the
//!   current into `.vcc` is 0 A to 2.7 mA;
//! - the gate driver's gate-to-source voltage, Table 6 "Electrical characteristics for VBUS
//!   (OCP, gate driver, current monitoring)" (printed page 6): `VGS` 4.5 V minimum, 5 V typical
//!   and 5.5 V maximum, with VBUSc 5 V to 20 V (`.gate_drive`);
//! - the VBUS overcurrent threshold across the sense resistor, the same table: `VTH_OCP_VBUS`
//!   35 mV minimum, 42 mV typical and 45 mV maximum (`.ocp_threshold`); the trip current is it
//!   over the board's sense resistor (section 7.5, printed page 13, "0.042 V across Rs").
//!
//! What is deliberately left out: the rest of Table 4, the absolute maximum ratings (Table 2:
//! `VCC_VCONN` 7 V, `VBUSc`, `Isense` and `SRC` 24 V, `CC1c` and `CC2c` 24 V), the overvoltage
//! thresholds, the current-sense gain, every register of the I2C interface (the address is set
//! by `I2C_ADD`), and the function of the part (no std generic is a USB-C protection IC, so the
//! part provides none and has no `dc` statement).
import std::sources::Rail

/// The TCPP02-M18 in QFN-18 with an exposed pad: a USB Type-C protection IC for a source, with
/// the CC lines' overvoltage protection, a gate driver for the VBUS switch, a VBUS current
/// monitor and an I2C interface. The pin names are the datasheet's and the pad numbers its pin
/// numbers (the exposed pad is 19). `.vcc` is the supply: `.vcc.pos` the `VCC_VCONN` pad and
/// `.vcc.neg` the `GND` pads.
part Tcpp02M18 {
    .designator &= "U"

    .vcc: Rail
    // Table 4, Recommended operating condition (printed page 5): VCC_VCONN 2.7 V to 5.5 V.
    .vcc.voltage >= 2.7V
    .vcc.voltage <= 5.5V
    // Table 5 (printed page 6): ICC_VCONN 2.7 mA at most in normal mode, 1 uA in low power mode.
    .vcc.current &= 0A..2.7mA

    /// The gate driver's voltage from `GATE` to `SRC`: 4.5 V to 5.5 V, 5 V typical (Table 6,
    /// printed page 6, VBUSc 5 V to 20 V). A board relates it to its switches'
    /// `.gate_source_voltage`.
    .gate_drive: Voltage
    .gate_drive &= 4.5V..5.5V

    /// The VBUS overcurrent threshold across the sense resistor between `VBUSc` and `Isense`:
    /// 35 mV to 45 mV, 42 mV typical (Table 6, printed page 6). The trip current is this over
    /// the board's sense resistor.
    .ocp_threshold: Voltage
    .ocp_threshold &= 35mV..45mV

    pins "QFN-18 (3.5x3.5)" {
        //  pin       kind           name         pads
        .en       input          "EN"         "1"
        .cc1      bidirectional  "CC1"        "2"
        .vcc.pos  power          "VCC_VCONN"  "3"
        .cc2      bidirectional  "CC2"        "4"
        .iana     output         "IANA"       "5"
        .gate     output         "GATE"       "6"
        .src      input          "SRC"        "7"
        .vbusc    input          "VBUSc"      "8"
        .isense   input          "Isense"     "9"
        .vcc.neg  power          "GND"        "10" "14" "19"
        .cc2c     bidirectional  "CC2c"       "11"
        .cbias    output         "CBIAS"      "12"
        .cc1c     bidirectional  "CC1c"       "13"
        .i2c_add  input          "I2C_ADD"    "15"
        .sda      bidirectional  "SDA"        "16"
        .scl      bidirectional  "SCL"        "17"
        .flgn     output         "FLGn"       "18"
    }

    .mpn: String
    .package: Package
    catalog tcpp02_m18 by .mpn { .mpn, .package }
}
